eding\" so it no longer contradicts the publish-round-trip non_goal. AC-001/002's \"truthy\" language was replaced with the exact guard predicate from action.yml:167. api_surface now specifies process substitution (not a pipe) and an explicit mkdir -p plus exit-terminating error handling per download, addressing the AC-003/AC-005(old) subshell-exit-swallowing finding directly in the mechanism description rather than leaving it to an implementer's guess. AC-007(old)/AC-005(new) narrows the callisto-publish-target ban to the example code block specifically, per the gate's first suggested option, since the status note's other claims (Java/.NET/the subcommand itself all still unimplemented) remain true and non-contradictory. New AC-008 closes the gate's final blocker: callisto-matrix.md §6.2's own reference snippet must be updated to match this spec's real mechanism, so the internal design doc and the shipped implementation don't silently diverge."
}

